---
title: Shape fixture
---

The document-shape pin: this file trips each `TAL-SHAPE-*` code exactly once, and its
sibling `skim-shape-clean.tmd` must trip none. The pair is what stops the rules from
passing vacuously — four of the five fire nowhere in the real corpus, so without a
deliberate fixture a broken rule would look identical to a clean one.

Each defect below is isolated on purpose: the rules overlap (an empty heading with nothing
under it is *also* hollow), so every section carries whatever content it needs to trip one
code and only one.

## Opening section

Prose, so this section is neither hollow nor a duplicate.

##

An unnamed heading trips `TAL-SHAPE-EMPTY`. This paragraph keeps it out of
`TAL-SHAPE-HOLLOW`, which would otherwise fire on the same line.

## Opening section

A second heading reading exactly like the first trips `TAL-SHAPE-DUP`. Prose again, so
hollow stays quiet.

## Shape fixture

A *body* heading restating the front-matter `title:` trips `TAL-SHAPE-ECHO`. The page's
leading heading is deliberately exempt, so the echo has to sit below one.

## A heading with nothing under it

## A closing section

The heading above has neither prose nor subsections, so it trips `TAL-SHAPE-HOLLOW` — and
because the next heading is at the *same* level, it is empty on any reading rather than an
ordinary grouping parent.

